Rules:

- A candidate is actionable only when it names ONE concrete change:
  which file or mechanism, what to change, the expected effect — all
  grounded in the observations. Drop friction too vague to name a
  change, drop praise, drop generic advice.
- Consolidate: observations pointing at the same file or mechanism
  merge into ONE candidate whose body carries one arm per observation
  (arm title, the concrete change, the expected effect).
- Title: short imperative, English. Body: what/where/effect, grounded
  in the observation text; the filing step appends the provenance
  lines, you do not write them.
- priority: 1 for high impact, 2 for normal.
- needs_user: true only when the change would add, change, or remove a
  tool, credential, or permission in an agent-reachable surface
  (environment variables, tool allowlists, hook or sandbox
  configuration, new binaries); otherwise false.
- source_seqs: the seqs this candidate distills.
- An empty array is a valid outcome: observations that name no concrete
  change produce nothing.

